00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:40.320
- [Instructor] The 2018
National Defense Strategy

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:42.180
articulates that the US military

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:44.190
will face increased global disorder,

00:02:44.190 --> 00:02:46.920
characterized by decline in
the long-standing rules-based

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:47.940
international order,

00:02:47.940 --> 00:02:51.270
creating a security environment
more complex and volatile

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:53.670
than any experience in recent memory.

00:02:53.670 --> 00:02:56.430
The reemergence of long-term
strategic competition,

00:02:56.430 --> 00:02:59.760
rapid dispersion of technologies
and new concepts of warfare

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:02.970
and competition that spans the
entire spectrum of conflict

00:03:02.970 --> 00:03:05.460
requires a joint force
to meet the challenges

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:06.393
of this reality.

00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:10.800
Adversaries anti-access area denial,

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:14.520
A2/AD capabilities aim to
create a broad area maritime

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:17.220
surveillance capability targeting system

00:03:17.220 --> 00:03:20.130
and contested Comms environment CCE,

00:03:20.130 --> 00:03:23.070
that in time of conflict would
render the existing naval

00:03:23.070 --> 00:03:26.223
and joint platform architecture
increasingly vulnerable.

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:30.630
Recognizing the increasingly
complex security environment

00:03:30.630 --> 00:03:33.540
the AI for maritime manure futures concept

00:03:33.540 --> 00:03:36.450
was designed to employ AI, Edge Compute,

00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:39.870
Specialized Communications
and robotic autonomy

00:03:39.870 --> 00:03:42.630
in maritime soft man/unmanned teams

00:03:42.630 --> 00:03:45.900
in a highly unique manner
to tip the balance of power

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:50.490
in multi-domain A2/80 competition
space to our advantage

00:03:50.490 --> 00:03:52.503
today and into the future.

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:56.370
Artificial intelligence for
maritime maneuver addresses

00:03:56.370 --> 00:03:59.730
those key problems faced in the
future operating environment

00:03:59.730 --> 00:04:02.640
to gain, maintain, and extend access

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:05.100
into the adversary's competition space.

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:07.920
While enabling the joint
forces decision advantage

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:10.410
and the application of scalable effects

00:04:10.410 --> 00:04:12.660
with enhanced precision.

00:04:12.660 --> 00:04:16.230
Hallmarks of the AIMM
concept, AI enabled SOF,

00:04:16.230 --> 00:04:20.940
maritime craft and seasoned
operators, Stealth, deception,

00:04:20.940 --> 00:04:24.330
mass and precision are intended
to penetrate the adversarial

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:28.740
defenses, complicate enemy kill
chains and ensure own force,

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:31.053
lethality and survivability.

00:04:31.980 --> 00:04:34.500
Future success will
increasingly go to the actor

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:36.240
who can best gather data,

00:04:36.240 --> 00:04:38.820
process it into actionable information

00:04:38.820 --> 00:04:43.590
and team with partners, both
human and machine in real time.

00:04:43.590 --> 00:04:47.430
Maritime SOF with specialized
low observable craft

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:50.700
and focused applications
of AI and autonomy

00:04:50.700 --> 00:04:53.520
teamed with multi-domain unmanned systems

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:56.610
can extend its access
swarming from the sea

00:04:56.610 --> 00:04:58.470
through the Lal commons in inland

00:04:58.470 --> 00:05:01.440
to directly enable
scalable and mass effects

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:03.363
on scene but unseen.

00:05:04.950 --> 00:05:07.050
The AIMM concept takes
advantage of cutting-edge

00:05:07.050 --> 00:05:10.890
usage of onboard compute,
data, artificial intelligence

00:05:10.890 --> 00:05:12.630
and specialized communications

00:05:12.630 --> 00:05:16.140
or AI-enabled mission
autonomy in small Uxs

00:05:16.140 --> 00:05:18.780
to deploy within range
of adversary targets

00:05:18.780 --> 00:05:21.373
enabling AI autonomous systems to detect,

00:05:21.373 --> 00:05:24.780
classify and identify IM points

00:05:24.780 --> 00:05:27.330
to provide enhanced precision of targeting

00:05:27.330 --> 00:05:31.113
to fires platforms enabling
a clear decision advantage.

00:05:31.980 --> 00:05:34.170
Critical to the success of these missions

00:05:34.170 --> 00:05:37.830
is all domain awareness, alternative PNT,

00:05:37.830 --> 00:05:41.730
mission autonomy and tactical
intelligence at the edge

00:05:41.730 --> 00:05:44.730
and specialized communications on demand,

00:05:44.730 --> 00:05:47.520
while ensuring mission
command deliberately

00:05:47.520 --> 00:05:50.970
and discreetly networked
to the joint force.

00:05:50.970 --> 00:05:54.090
Given their low observable
small size mission autonomy,

00:05:54.090 --> 00:05:56.280
and tactical intelligence at the edge,

00:05:56.280 --> 00:05:58.020
AI enabled robotic systems

00:05:58.020 --> 00:06:00.570
in maritime SOF man/unmanned teams

00:06:00.570 --> 00:06:03.330
are uniquely positioned
to excel in their ability

00:06:03.330 --> 00:06:06.810
to gain, maintain, and extend access

00:06:06.810 --> 00:06:09.153
into highly contested environments.

00:06:10.230 --> 00:06:14.400
An on above and under maritime
SOF sea strike portfolio

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:18.570
of access mass and precision
could provide the joint force

00:06:18.570 --> 00:06:20.790
with a broader spectrum of unique options

00:06:20.790 --> 00:06:24.753
to create more complex dilemmas
for defeating adversaries.

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:29.370
AIMM expands the maritime
strike Warfare's ability

00:06:29.370 --> 00:06:32.670
to achieve kinetic effects on
a broader variety of targets

00:06:32.670 --> 00:06:35.490
that might have otherwise
been inaccessible.

00:06:35.490 --> 00:06:37.860
AIMM promises to shrink
the competition bubble

00:06:37.860 --> 00:06:40.740
in highly contested A2/AD environments

00:06:40.740 --> 00:06:44.940
by employing AI enabled
maritime SOF man/unmanned teams

00:06:44.940 --> 00:06:47.550
operating far forward in
contested environments

00:06:47.550 --> 00:06:50.580
to deliver kinetic and
non-kinetic effects,

00:06:50.580 --> 00:06:53.250
including unprecedented access to SUB-T

00:06:53.250 --> 00:06:54.570
and mobile launch sites.

00:06:54.570 --> 00:06:57.840
Ultimately removing cover and
concealment from our opponents

00:06:57.840 --> 00:07:01.350
while providing targeting
quality data to the joint force.

00:07:01.350 --> 00:07:03.900
AI for automated target detection,

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:07.230
tracking, cross-cueuing
and command and control

00:07:07.230 --> 00:07:08.670
will further expand the ways

00:07:08.670 --> 00:07:11.940
in which the maritime
soft man/unmanned team

00:07:11.940 --> 00:07:15.240
can enable joint warfare
with speed, precision,

00:07:15.240 --> 00:07:18.783
and mass efficiency to support
the effects kill chain.

00:07:19.740 --> 00:07:22.710
The artificial intelligence
for maritime maneuver futures

00:07:22.710 --> 00:07:26.520
concept leverages maritime
soft capabilities envisioned

00:07:26.520 --> 00:07:29.130
to operate in new and
unique ways when empowered

00:07:29.130 --> 00:07:32.010
by AI autonomous systems to operate

00:07:32.010 --> 00:07:34.770
in maritime SOF man/unmanned teams

00:07:34.770 --> 00:07:37.380
to solve critical operational problems

00:07:37.380 --> 00:07:39.633
of the future operating environment.

00:07:40.590 --> 00:07:44.160
The AI enabled maritime
SOF man/unmanned team

00:07:44.160 --> 00:07:48.060
provides a collection of
unique, scalable capabilities

00:07:48.060 --> 00:07:51.240
that will enable the joint
force to compete and win

00:07:51.240 --> 00:07:54.060
in complex, contested
and denied environments

00:07:54.060 --> 00:07:56.400
across the competition continuum.

00:07:56.400 --> 00:07:59.705
This is what the nation expects
from special operations.

